OL,3,GNEWSA'Racist comments not acceptable' -
OL,4,Acafe owner speaks out over long-running
OL,5,Aabuse
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe owner of a kebab shop has spoken
OL,8,Fout about long-running racist abuse her
OL,9,Fand her family have been subjected to
OL,10,Fduring 30 years of being in business.
OL,12,FSaba Asghar-Rahman, the owner of The
OL,13,FFab Kebab Bistro in Ballymoney, County
OL,14,FAntrim, said racism was "not
OL,15,Facceptable" after a recent incident in
OL,16,Fwhich her husband was abused while
OL,17,Fworking in the cafe.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,417,410,260,120,0,100
